  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building Tuberculosis Control Capacity with Community-based mHealth approach in Nouakchott, Mauritanie</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mobile DOTS in mHealth is implemented by 1) installing Smart pillboxes at tuberculosis patients&apos; houses, 2) conducting group voice phones calls for following check ups, 3) collecting tuberculosis data through computerized patient management program(MIDMS), and periodically 4)  educating medical,public health staffs about mHealth. To strengthen community capacity, 1) leaders of regional association gets  training, 2) community awareness campaigns are held, and 3) CHWs make tuberculosis patients and family visits (for TB education, supporting low-income families, and active case finding).</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project aims to improve the tuberculosis(TB) control governance system using mHealth in all areas of Nuakshott, the capital of Mauritania. Purpose of the project is to reduce PDV rate(increase in tuberculosis treatment success rate) and strengthen the community&apos;s ability to manage tuberculosis(TB).1. mHealth&#xB97C; &#xD1B5;&#xD55C; &#xACB0;&#xD575;&#xAD00;&#xB9AC;&#xC758; &#xAC1C;&#xC120;
2. &#xC9C0;&#xC5ED;&#xC0AC;&#xD68C; &#xC5ED;&#xB7C9;&#xAC15;&#xD654;</narrative>
  </description>
